{% set local_problem %}
<p>Alabama's humidity takes a toll on fascia boards. When gutters clog or leak, water soaks into the fascia. In our humid climate, that moisture creates perfect conditions for rot, mold, and wood-destroying insects.</p>

<p>Tanner homes of all ages can have fascia problems. Established homes have weathered decades of exposure. Even newer construction can develop issues if gutters weren't properly installed or maintained.</p>

<p>Fascia problems are common — and commonly missed. Homeowners call about gutter issues, and we find the real problem is the rotted wood behind the gutters. You can't fix gutters without fixing fascia first.</p>

<p>Caught early, fascia repair is straightforward. Left alone, rot spreads to rafters and roof structure.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We start with a thorough inspection for water damage, soft spots, and rot. We'll show you exactly what we find.</p>

<p>For damaged sections, we remove gutters, cut out rotted wood back to solid material, and install new fascia boards using quality materials designed for our humid climate.</p>

<p>Everything is sealed and prepared for gutter installation. Then we install seamless gutters designed to prevent the overflow that caused the rot.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been repairing fascia throughout North Alabama for over 20 years. We serve the Athens-Decatur corridor regularly, so Tanner is part of our territory.</p>

<p>When you hire Blue River Gutters, you're hiring a company that knows this area and will do the job right.</p>
{% endset %}

